			"notes": "Fruit Fly: A Small Mind brings a simplified spiking simulation on measured FlyWire connectivity into Minecraft Java 26.2.\n\n- 138,639 modeled neurons and 15,091,983 directed connection records.\n- Custom fruit fly mob, spawn egg, fermenting fruit bowl, capture bottle, and developmental stages.\n- Fermentation-based habitat, feeding, reproduction, resting, escape, and frog predation.\n- Live brain overlay: **B** toggle, **N** next fly, **R** freeze/resume rotation.\n\n### Download and play\n\nDownload **FruitFly-26.2.zip** for the mod, matching Fabric API, installation instructions, and license notices. Alternatively download **fruitfly-1.0.0.jar** and supply Fabric API 0.160.0+26.2 separately.\n\nRequires Minecraft Java **26.2**, Fabric Loader **0.19.5+**, and **Java 25**. Install the mod and Fabric API on both client and server. Blender and Python are not required to play.\n\n### What the brain does\n\nMeasured connectivity drives a simplified neural simulation whose outputs modulate turning, speed, and escape. Navigation and ecology also use programmed rules. This is a hybrid computational model, not a validated complete biological fly simulation. The overlay displays a 1,200-neuron anatomical sample with actual simulated spike activity.\n\n### Verification\n\nLocal verification passed: 12 server GameTests, a rendered client integration test, and the full-network benchmark with sampled graph-integrity checks. See the repository's verification summary and GitHub Actions for build results.\n\nOriginal code and artwork: MIT. Bundled FlyWire-derived data: **CC BY-NC 4.0**; preserve attribution and its noncommercial restriction. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. SHA-256 checksums are provided for downloadable artifacts."
